                                "sense_id": "e54b7681-92c0-3b8b-b58d-808c964f7ea9",
                                "text": "1642, Thomas Morton, The Presentment of a Schismaticke, London: R. Whitaker & S. Brown, p. 6,\nI have reserved for the last place a Character which maketh his case most desperate, called by Auusten maddish obstinacy […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34e36104-edc1-4c48-a3c4-acdb334c0d9e",
                                "sense_id": "e54b7681-92c0-3b8b-b58d-808c964f7ea9",
                                "text": "1815, Charles Lamb, letter to William Wordsworth dated 28 April, 1815, in The Letters of Charles Lamb, Boston: The Bibliophile Society, 1905, Volume 4, p. 39,\nExcuse this maddish letter: I am too tired to write in forma."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f08d4a8-db91-475d-8f86-8763d9328f02",
                                "sense_id": "e54b7681-92c0-3b8b-b58d-808c964f7ea9",
                                "text": "He is small and thin, and has glasses and large teeth and the maddish smile of genuine intellectual passion."
                            }
                        ]
